    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64090,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Uterus and extrauterine sites in metastatic disease</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64091,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Vaginal bleeding with persistent elevation of serum hCG after primary evacuation of a hydatidiform mole is characteristic {3010701; 25318458; 25607129}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64092,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>No epidemiological data are available.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64093,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the majority of cases, invasive moles develop from complete hydatidiform moles {26535984}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64094,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64095,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion consists of invasive molar tissue extending into the myometrium. Hydropic villi may be visible, and uterine perforation may occur.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64096,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most invasive hydatidiform moles are complete hydatidiform moles, which retain the villous histological characteristics but demonstrate myometrial and/or vascular invasion. Invasive partial moles also occur {25318458; 8737309}. In cases of metastatic mole, the features are those of complete hydatidiform molar villi in extrauterine locations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64097,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64098,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64099,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> villi with abnormal trophoblastic proliferation within myometrium and/or uterine or extrauterine vessels.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64100,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>See <em>TNM staging of gestational trophoblastic neoplasms</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]].</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:55:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64101,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In the absence of immediate complications (e.g. severe haemorrhage), chemotherapy is highly effective, with a cure rate of &gt;&nbsp;80%, depending on the extent of the disease {19369669; 26535984; 25607129}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-03T17:53:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
